                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6359c70c-515a-43e5-bd86-2a7887a7e5c2",
                        "source_entry_id": "d666f218-47a2-3ee0-b067-e0999370dcb0",
                        "source_sense_id": "98863122-679c-3eb2-b2a9-377a7761134a",
                        "target_lang_word": "furiously",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "furiously",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ccf81bb-3f27-330a-9bbb-aae9a183b40e",
                                        "entry_id": "4c81731a-8a06-3b24-a8bf-48273aebd489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a furious manner; angrily."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "826b4f75-bb02-4cc8-abd7-5458c8ee2f6d",
                                                "sense_id": "2ccf81bb-3f27-330a-9bbb-aae9a183b40e",
                                                "text": "He glared furiously at the offender."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5244078a-9891-4059-ab2f-e4b5346cb44f",
                                                "sense_id": "2ccf81bb-3f27-330a-9bbb-aae9a183b40e",
                                                "text": "Case in point, as Lichfield detailed on Twitter last week: Almost as soon as the \"hipster effect\" article was published, a man furiously emailed the magazine claiming a photo of him was slanderously used alongside it without his permission. He was, it turned out, mistaken."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60e3e782-3be6-3bf8-9431-a1ccc629c3cf",
                                        "entry_id": "4c81731a-8a06-3b24-a8bf-48273aebd489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Quickly; frantically; with great effort or speed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3a80681-6e29-49a3-a71a-1cc994acf1d6",
                                                "sense_id": "60e3e782-3be6-3bf8-9431-a1ccc629c3cf",
                                                "text": "He tried furiously to get it to work before the deadline."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "804f443d-80bf-4936-8c18-416ced1f0a56",
                                                "sense_id": "60e3e782-3be6-3bf8-9431-a1ccc629c3cf",
                                                "text": "Again we set to and bailed furiously. Fortunately the storm had now quite gone by[.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1884d23-f9e3-45ca-8c28-9685c288e9d5",
                                                "sense_id": "60e3e782-3be6-3bf8-9431-a1ccc629c3cf",
                                                "text": "“It was nonsense to pretend that he was afraid of the scandal, as no possible scandal could attach to him. This attitude of his gave me furiously to think, and I was slowly forced to the conclusion that Alfred Inglethorp wanted to be arrested.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0ce8893-4d45-354a-aa64-64afe76dbe9f",
                                        "entry_id": "4c81731a-8a06-3b24-a8bf-48273aebd489",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Intensely, as with embarrassment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57dbe89a-7a93-49e4-a202-1d47b1a961d2",
                                                "sense_id": "c0ce8893-4d45-354a-aa64-64afe76dbe9f",
                                                "text": "Craig, who at twenty was taller than his father, blushed furiously as he practically threw two small boxes on the table in front of the twins. “Happy birthday”, he managed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6bccec87-eab4-49f3-b2ff-f7495f18baa3",
                        "source_entry_id": "d666f218-47a2-3ee0-b067-e0999370dcb0",
                        "source_sense_id": "98863122-679c-3eb2-b2a9-377a7761134a",
                        "target_lang_word": "frantically",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "frantically",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80b7c301-d02d-3979-86f1-8ea5deb58dbd",
                                        "entry_id": "4b4d82ae-fc57-3015-94e3-09306c12912f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a frantic way."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e51d35cb-9505-4920-b63c-3fc4b9d1a894",
                                                "sense_id": "80b7c301-d02d-3979-86f1-8ea5deb58dbd",
                                                "text": "He searched frantically for his passport before the flight."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff4d2ce6-caa0-4ef7-81fa-fd18dd7020b3",
                                                "sense_id": "80b7c301-d02d-3979-86f1-8ea5deb58dbd",
                                                "text": "For quotations using this term, see Citations:frantically."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "09c8bce5-d0ee-4603-8f97-3afb8796e442",
                        "source_entry_id": "d666f218-47a2-3ee0-b067-e0999370dcb0",
                        "source_sense_id": "98863122-679c-3eb2-b2a9-377a7761134a",
                        "target_lang_word": "passionately",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "passionately",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bec69e54-3cb8-3897-b154-127d2008a100",
                                        "entry_id": "f7081c0d-aa9c-3e7b-b989-4532101928a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a passionate manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e8e14ab-81a4-4a34-bbd6-86cdeb2d89d1",
                                                "sense_id": "bec69e54-3cb8-3897-b154-127d2008a100",
                                                "text": "“The story of this adoption is, of course, the pivot round which all the circumstances of the mysterious tragedy revolved. Mrs. Yule had an only son, namely, William, to whom she was passionately attached ; but, like many a fond mother, she had the desire of mapping out that son's future entirely according to her own ideas.[…]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a62cd9b0-a947-463e-8087-623cb5f902f4",
                                                "sense_id": "bec69e54-3cb8-3897-b154-127d2008a100",
                                                "text": "And it was while all were passionately intent upon the pleasing and snake-like progress of their uncle that a young girl in furs, ascending the stairs two at a time, peeped perfunctorily into the nursery as she passed the hallway—and halted amazed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36f010e6-4648-4c28-a0ca-9f09480e2f8c",
                                                "sense_id": "bec69e54-3cb8-3897-b154-127d2008a100",
                                                "text": "Was the sorrow at Mrs. Inglethorp’s death so great? I realized that there was an emotional lack in the atmosphere. The dead woman had not the gift of commanding love. Her death was a shock and a distress, but she would not be passionately regretted."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "36f0593f-ffc0-4288-afa7-e19ab3cf0d89",
                        "source_entry_id": "d666f218-47a2-3ee0-b067-e0999370dcb0",
                        "source_sense_id": "98863122-679c-3eb2-b2a9-377a7761134a",
                        "target_lang_word": "violently",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
